  "aciklama": "Saudia 163 landed after a cargo fire, but no one escaped. The cause: cabin fire and smoke with evacuation never started after landing.\n\nFailure chain: Smoke warning in cargo hold → Slow return to airport → Lands and taxis → Doors not opened → Fire and smoke fill cabin\n\nAnother reconstruction: The Disaster That Ended the Age of the Airship — https://youtu.be/PGOKZhPYo7c\n\nFootage & sources:\n• Archival film: \"Saudia Flight 163 aftermath of fire onboard.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saudia_Flight_163_aftermath_of_fire_onboard.jpg\n• Archival film: \"Tail wreckage of HZ-AHK.png\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tail_wreckage_of_HZ-AHK.png\n• Archival film: \"Saudia Flight 163 Wreckage 1984.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saudia_Flight_163_Wreckage_1984.jpg\n\nTechnical references:\n• Wikipedia — Saudia Flight 163 — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saudia_Flight_163\n• FAA — AircraftAccidentReportSAA (cited by Wikipedia) — https://www.faa.gov/sites/faa.gov/files/AircraftAccidentReportSAA.pdf\n\nNarration uses a synthetic voice. Footage is real archival film or licensed stock; anything reconstructed is labelled on screen.\n\nFailure File · Episode 16 · A new engineering failure, reconstructed every day.\n\n#shorts #engineering #Saudia163 #firesafety #history",
